From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] client: bare_app: the window as drawn, for the stream

While bare_app streams the screen (rtsp://...:8554/live) it asks the
game for its own picture (game_ipc.h: full_want), and the stream takes
that instead of the screen: the window as VCMI drew it, not taken down
to the handheld's screen. The default view draws at twice the frame and
halves it: its whole screen at 1:1 (960x640 for the 480x320 frame of the
ODROID-GO Advance), the magnifier's too. The native view's is its whole
screen as well. The fit view (BARE_APP_VCMI_FIT) draws at twice its
window and takes it down to the frame: the window is that screen taken
down 2:1 by a second Downscaler, in linear light and only the rows that
changed, like the frame (854x600 on the GO Ultra). Nothing when it is no
bigger than the frame. The cursor is drawn over it at its own size, the
colour scheme applied too. It is published before each frame, a frame
all the same too, so the stream keeps its size over a still picture.
Nothing of it while nobody watches: the second Downscaler and its copy
of the screen go.

